# MySQL Rules

- Normalize schema based on domain needs and access patterns.
- Add indexes for frequent filters, joins, and ordering.
- Prevent N+1 queries through eager loading or query redesign.
- Use foreign keys to protect referential integrity.
- Plan for scalability (pagination, selective columns, batching).
- Use soft deletes only when business requirements need recoverability.
